        "updated_at": "2023-05-15T21:55:08Z",
        "body": "That was fast. I just found that I could iterate through the videos and add \".json\" to them and then do this command:\r\n\r\nmy_list = drive.ListFile({'q': f\"title='nusar-2021_action_both_9011-b06b_9011_user_id_2021-02-01_154253.json'\"}).GetList()\r\n\r\nAnd then the json showed up ^_^.\r\n\r\nEDIT: for anyone who wants easy mode this might work:\r\n\r\n```\r\n    jsons = list(set([x.split('/')[0] for x in master_dict.keys()]))\r\n    json_objs = []\r\n    for x in jsons:\r\n        json_objs = drive.ListFile({'q': f\"title='{x}.json'\"}).GetList()\r\n        if len(json_objs) > 0:\r\n            json_objs[0].GetContentFile(json_objs[0]['title'])\r\n```",
